{%- comment -%} ====================== HOW IT WORKS ====================== {%- endcomment -%}
<section class="section" id="how-it-works"><div class="wrap">
  <div class="center">
    <span class="eyebrow" data-reveal>How it works</span>
    <h2 data-reveal style="--reveal-delay:60ms">Open it. Navigate it. Find anything.</h2>
    <p class="lead" data-reveal style="--reveal-delay:120ms">Every file is memory-mapped and parsed once into a compact index &mdash; only the rows on screen are ever built.</p>
  </div>

  {%- comment -%} pipeline diagram: disk -> mmap -> index -> viewport {%- endcomment -%}
  <div data-reveal="zoom" style="margin-top:52px">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 1080 200" width="100%" role="img" aria-label="Pipeline: the file stays on disk, is memory-mapped, indexed at 24 bytes per node, and only the visible rows are built." style="display:block;max-width:980px;margin:0 auto;overflow:hidden">
      <defs>
        <linearGradient id="pipeWarm" x1="0" y1="0" x2="1" y2="0">
          <stop offset="0%" stop-color="#E87C4D"/><stop offset="100%" stop-color="#F2A166"/>
        </linearGradient>
        <linearGradient id="pipeFlow" x1="0" y1="0" x2="1" y2="0">
          <stop offset="0%" stop-color="#E87C4D" stop-opacity="0"/>
          <stop offset="50%" stop-color="#F2A166" stop-opacity="1"/>
          <stop offset="100%" stop-color="#4C9DF7" stop-opacity="0"/>
        </linearGradient>
      </defs>

      <line x1="60" y1="100" x2="1020" y2="100" stroke="#2F3B55" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="5 7"/>
      <line x1="60" y1="100" x2="1020" y2="100" stroke="url(#pipeFlow)" stroke-width="3" stroke-dasharray="130 830" stroke-linecap="round">
        <animate attributeName="stroke-dashoffset" from="960" to="-130" dur="4s" repeatCount="indefinite"/>
      </line>

      <g font-family="JetBrains Mono, monospace">
        <!-- 1. on disk -->
        <g transform="translate(60,52)">
          <rect width="176" height="96" rx="14" fill="#131826" stroke="#222B3E"/>
          <rect x="18" y="20" width="34" height="42" rx="5" fill="none" stroke="#E87C4D" stroke-width="2"/>
          <path d="M24 32h22M24 40h22M24 48h14" stroke="#E87C4D" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" opacity=".75"/>
          <text x="64" y="38" fill="#EDF1F7" font-size="14" font-weight="700">8.4 GB</text>
          <text x="64" y="57" fill="#7A87A5" font-size="11">stays on disk</text>
          <text x="18" y="82" fill="#7A87A5" font-size="10" letter-spacing="1.4">01 · SOURCE</text>
        </g>

        <!-- 2. memory map -->
        <g transform="translate(292,52)">
          <rect width="176" height="96" rx="14" fill="#131826" stroke="#222B3E"/>
          <g stroke="#4C9DF7" stroke-width="2" fill="none">
            <rect x="18" y="24" width="15" height="15" rx="3"/><rect x="37" y="24" width="15" height="15" rx="3"/>
            <rect x="18" y="43" width="15" height="15" rx="3"/><rect x="37" y="43" width="15" height="15" rx="3" opacity=".4"/>
          </g>
          <text x="64" y="38" fill="#EDF1F7" font-size="14" font-weight="700">mmap</text>
          <text x="64" y="57" fill="#7A87A5" font-size="11">zero copy</text>
          <text x="18" y="82" fill="#7A87A5" font-size="10" letter-spacing="1.4">02 · MAP</text>
        </g>

        <!-- 3. structural index -->
        <g transform="translate(524,52)">
          <rect width="176" height="96" rx="14" fill="#131826" stroke="#222B3E"/>
          <g stroke="#3DD68C" stroke-width="2" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round">
            <path d="M20 28h10M20 38h10M20 48h10M20 58h10"/>
            <path d="M34 28h14M34 38h18M34 48h12M34 58h16" opacity=".45"/>
          </g>
          <text x="64" y="38" fill="#EDF1F7" font-size="14" font-weight="700">24 B / node</text>
          <text x="64" y="57" fill="#7A87A5" font-size="11">structural index</text>
          <text x="20" y="82" fill="#7A87A5" font-size="10" letter-spacing="1.4">03 · INDEX</text>
        </g>

        <!-- 4. viewport -->
        <g transform="translate(756,52)">
          <rect width="264" height="96" rx="14" fill="#131826" stroke="url(#pipeWarm)" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <g stroke="#F2A166" stroke-width="2" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round">
            <path d="M22 30h9M22 42h9M22 54h9"/>
            <path d="M37 30h20M37 42h28M37 54h16"/>
          </g>
          <text x="76" y="38" fill="#EDF1F7" font-size="14" font-weight="700">~40 rows built</text>
          <text x="76" y="57" fill="#7A87A5" font-size="11">cost tracks the viewport</text>
          <text x="22" y="82" fill="#F2A166" font-size="10" letter-spacing="1.4">04 · VIEWPORT</text>
        </g>
      </g>
    </svg>
  </div>

  <div class="steps" data-stagger="100">
    <div class="step"><div class="step__n">1</div><h3>Open the file</h3><p>Drag in a JSON, NDJSON, XML, CSV or TSV file up to 10+ GB (50+ GB with 32&ndash;64 GB of RAM) &mdash; or paste from the clipboard or fetch a URL with auth. It opens instantly, no progress bars.</p></div>
    <div class="step"><div class="step__n">2</div><h3>Navigate the tree</h3><p>Everything renders as one uniform, virtualized tree. Jump to any path, bookmark nodes, and read collapsed counts like &ldquo;products : […], 31 items&rdquo;.</p></div>
    <div class="step"><div class="step__n">3</div><h3>Search &amp; export</h3><p>Regex find, live filter, or JSONPath / XPath queries backed by parallel native search. Then export or convert to JSON, XML or CSV.</p></div>
  </div>
</div></section>

