{%- comment -%} ======================== FEATURES ======================== {%- endcomment -%}
<section class="section section--alt" id="features"><div class="wrap">
  <div class="center">
    <span class="eyebrow" data-reveal>Everything you need</span>
    <h2 data-reveal style="--reveal-delay:60ms">A data workbench, <span class="grad-text">not a text editor.</span></h2>
    <p class="lead" data-reveal style="--reveal-delay:120ms">Browse, query, transform and convert your files like a database &mdash; with the tools you'd expect from an enterprise DBMS.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="features" data-stagger="70">

    <div class="feature"><div class="feature__ic"><svg width="23" height="23" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 4h7"/><path d="M6 4v14a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h2"/><path d="M6 12h4"/><rect x="13" y="2" width="8" height="5" rx="1.5"/><rect x="13" y="10" width="8" height="5" rx="1.5"/><rect x="13" y="18" width="8" height="4" rx="1.5"/></svg></div><h3>Virtualized tree view</h3><p>Objects, arrays, XML elements and CSV records render in one uniform, collapsible tree. Cost per frame tracks visible rows (~40), never file size.</p></div>

    <div class="feature"><div class="feature__ic"><svg width="23" height="23" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="10.5" cy="10.5" r="6.5"/><path d="m16 16 5 5"/><path d="M8 10.5h5M10.5 8v5"/></svg></div><h3>Lightning search</h3><p>Trigram-indexed literal or regex search scoped to keys, values or attributes &mdash; finds anything in milliseconds, even on massive files.</p></div>

    <div class="feature"><div class="feature__ic"><svg width="23" height="23" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M8 3H7a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v4a2 2 0 0 1-2 2 2 2 0 0 1 2 2v4a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h1"/><path d="M16 3h1a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v4a2 2 0 0 0 2 2 2 2 0 0 0-2 2v4a2 2 0 0 1-2 2h-1"/><path d="M12 9v6"/></svg></div><h3>JSONPath, XPath &amp; jq</h3><p>Query JSON/CSV with <code>$.store.items[*].name</code> and XML with <code>//item/@id</code>, or run a full <code>jq</code> program in the built-in bar &mdash; results open in a new tab.</p></div>

    <div class="feature"><div class="feature__ic"><svg width="23" height="23" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m12 2 9 5-9 5-9-5Z"/><path d="m3 12 9 5 9-5"/><path d="m3 17 9 5 9-5"/></svg></div><h3>Dual-engine architecture</h3><p>Two engines in one &mdash; in-memory for speed, database-scale for the biggest files &mdash; auto-selected for your data. Files too large to index eagerly still open on demand.</p></div>

    <div class="feature"><div class="feature__ic"><svg width="23" height="23" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="3" y="4" width="18" height="16" rx="2"/><path d="M3 9h18M3 14.5h18M9 9v11M15 9v11"/></svg></div><h3>Spreadsheet-grade tables</h3><p>Pin, filter, sort and profile millions of rows like a spreadsheet, with a SQL console over CSV, TSV and delimited files. Leading-zero cells like ZIP codes stay strings.</p></div>

    <div class="feature"><div class="feature__ic"><svg width="23" height="23" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2 12h4l2.5 7 4-16L15 12h7"/></svg></div><h3>Follow tail (tail -f)</h3><p>Follow a growing JSON / NDJSON / log file. Only newly appended lines are parsed each tick, so it stays cheap on huge, live files.</p></div>

    <div class="feature"><div class="feature__ic"><svg width="23" height="23" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 8h14l-3.5-3.5"/><path d="M21 16H7l3.5 3.5"/></svg></div><h3>Every format, one click</h3><p>JSON, NDJSON, XML, YAML, CSV, TSV and delimited files in one app &mdash; convert freely between them, batch-export, or save your search matches as a dataset.</p></div>

    <div class="feature"><div class="feature__ic"><svg width="23" height="23" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/><path d="M3 12h18"/><path d="M12 3a15 15 0 0 1 0 18 15 15 0 0 1 0-18Z"/></svg></div><h3>Integrated API workbench</h3><p>Postman-style requests with None / Basic / Bearer / API-Key auth &mdash; explore live responses as structured data and copy any request as cURL.</p></div>

    <div class="feature"><div class="feature__ic"><svg width="23" height="23" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 21h18"/><rect x="4" y="12" width="4" height="7" rx="1"/><rect x="10" y="7" width="4" height="12" rx="1"/><rect x="16" y="3" width="4" height="16" rx="1"/></svg></div><h3>Schema, diff &amp; insight</h3><p>Generate and validate schemas, diff two files, check column coverage, and read child counts, type histograms and numeric min / max / avg for any node.</p></div>

  </div>
</div></section>

