{%- comment -%} ========================== FAQ ========================== {%- endcomment -%}
<section class="section" id="faq"><div class="wrap">
  <div class="center">
    <span class="eyebrow" data-reveal>Questions, answered</span>
    <h2 data-reveal style="--reveal-delay:60ms">What to know before you download.</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="faq" data-faq data-stagger="60">
    <details open><summary>How large a file can NARIKJSON really open?</summary><p>On a typical machine it&#39;s comfortable around 10 GB. With 32&ndash;64 GB of RAM it opens 50+ GB files and hundreds of millions of rows &mdash; performance scales with the memory you give it. Files too large to index eagerly fall back to the database engine and on-demand indexing, so documents near or beyond your available RAM still open.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Which formats are supported?</summary><p>JSON, JSON-Lines / NDJSON, XML, YAML, CSV, TSV and other delimited files &mdash; all in one app, with one-click conversion between them. You can also paste from the clipboard or open from a URL.</p></details>
    <details><summary>What are the two engines?</summary><p>NARIKJSON runs an in-memory engine for speed and a database engine for scale, and picks the right one for your file automatically. The database engine uses SQLite for JSON and XML and DuckDB for CSV and delimited data, which is what makes multi-GB files and 100M+ rows practical.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Does my data leave my machine?</summary><p>No. Files are processed locally by the native Rust core. Nothing is uploaded &mdash; the only network calls are the ones you make yourself from the API workbench.</p></details>
    <details><summary>What platforms does it run on?</summary><p>macOS (Apple Silicon and Intel) and Linux today. A Windows build is coming soon &mdash; <a href="{{ pages.contact.url | default: '/pages/contact' }}">get notified</a>.</p></details>
    <details><summary>What&#39;s the difference between the free and paid tiers?</summary><p>They are the same complete application. NARIKJSON Free is billed monthly at no cost; the paid NARIKJSON license is billed yearly and adds volume and site licensing, managed deployment, centralized updates and a dedicated support SLA for teams.</p></details>
  </div>
</div></section>

